# Aislix Chart Map

Follow `aislix-visual-design-system.mdc`. Adjacency cycle: PURPLE → BLUE → PINK → GREEN → CYAN.

## Audit performance
- Completion trend → **line** PURPLE `#9B86D9` (prior period = grey)
- Outcome → **donut** Pass GREEN / Fail PINK / Incomplete GREY; center = pass %

## Findings & actions
- By severity → **stacked h-bar** Critical PINK · High darker pink · Medium BLUE · Low GREY
- Findings trend → **line** CYAN; optional critical series PINK
- Corrective status → **stacked h-bar** Open BLUE · In Progress PURPLE · Completed GREEN · Overdue PINK

## Planogram / execution
- Compliance by store → **ranked h-bar** PURPLE, worst→best, target ref line if configured
- Top SKU facing gaps → **ranked h-bar** CYAN, largest shortfall first
- Brand share of facings → **h-bar** GREEN focus brand; others light grey; expected = grey marker
- Category share → **h-bar** BLUE; unavailable = grey empty (never invent mapping)

## Product intelligence
- Top by facings → **ranked h-bar** PURPLE, Brand → Product → Variant
- Top by units → **ranked h-bar** CYAN (same naming; never `Product · UNVERIFIABLE`)

## Brand / category comparison
- Brand facing vs unit share → **grouped h-bar** GREEN + CYAN
- Category facing vs unit share → **grouped h-bar** BLUE + PURPLE

## Inventory
- Unit shortfall → expected GREY + actual CYAN
- Potential visible-unit value gap → **h-bar** CYAN (not "loss/theft")
- Visible shelf coverage days → **h-bar** BLUE (+ grey threshold)

## Price / promo (only if Luna returned data)
- MRP vs selling → **grouped h-bar** BLUE + PURPLE
- Promotion presence → GREEN; none = grey empty

## Financial
- Potential Daily Value at Risk → KPI + optional columns CYAN
- Potential Weekly Value at Risk → KPI + optional columns PURPLE
- Value impact by SKU → **h-bar** CYAN

## Confidence / quality
- AI confidence → **progress bars** BLUE (threshold tints only if backend defines them)
- Image quality → status card GOOD GREEN · LIMITED BLUE · POOR PINK (not a chart)

## Empty / mismatch
Unavailable → title + "Data unavailable" + one-line why (GREY). COUNT_MISMATCH → "COUNT VERIFICATION PENDING", aggregates not as normal numbers.
